  "result": "Don't train a model for this: training and model math are outside your mission, and you have about three hours a week. RL (reinforcement learning, which trains by rewarding good outcomes) is used to train some models, but a good assistant doesn't require training your own.\n\nA PPO derivation is too big for a chat reply. [OpenAI's Spinning Up PPO page](https://spinningup.openai.com/en/latest/algorithms/ppo.html), under \"Key Equations\", gives the objective and links to a note on its simplified form.\n\nFor better tool use, start by finding where it fails. Say a ski-rental assistant fails 5 of 20 test requests:\n\n| Step | Finding | Why it matters |\n|---|---|---|\n| Write the pass rule first | \"Books the right date and size\" | Makes grading consistent |\n| Run all 20 | 15 pass | Gives a baseline |\n| Group failures | 3 wrong dates, 2 wrong sizes | Shows what to inspect first |\n| Inspect the date cases | Today's date was never given to the model | Points to a fix without training |\n| Fix and rerun all 20 | Compare with 15 | Catches new breakage |\n\nWhat are three real student requests, with pass rules, that you'd put in your makerspace test set?",
